CORE
dsb.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model reg:observe --mmio-weak --mmio-early-ack
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
the write has completed after the barrier: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
A full fence is a completion barrier (ARM DSB): it completes posted writes, so
after it the write to reg has landed and the assertion holds. Compare test.desc,
where a lightweight fence (DMB) does not complete the write.
